WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740
Now that we have covered the legal protections in place,

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.440
let's look at what this looks like in the real world.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.240
On the screen is a video titled Life and Death Drama.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.340
As we watch this, I want you to notice

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.120
that sudden cardiac arrest can truly happen to anyone,

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.120
regardless of their age, race, gender, or demographic.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.400
Even though there are often stereotypes

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.799
about who is at risk,

00:00:23.799 --> 00:00:26.139
these examples show that cardiac arrest

00:00:26.139 --> 00:00:30.660
does not discriminate and can happen to anyone at any time.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.939
I want you to notice a specific detail

00:00:32.939 --> 00:00:35.220
in how these individuals fall.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.419
Notice that they do not put out their hands

00:00:37.419 --> 00:00:38.820
to brace themselves.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.459
This is because cardiac arrest

00:00:40.459 --> 00:00:43.900
causes the heart to stop pumping blood immediately.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.980
Because blood flow to the brain is cut off instantly,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.660
the person loses consciousness

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.540
and collapses without any warning or time to react.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.540
Recognizing this sudden unprotected collapse

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.660
is a key way for you to identify

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.820
that someone needs your help right away.

